  When `fSevereTransfer` is true and a collected `SinkRatio` is already above `ABC_STMAP58_BOUND_RATIO_CAP`, this initializes `BoundedRatio` with that unbounded value while the cap is only applied to the raw `Candidate`; if the sink fallback remains larger, ratios above the advertised 2.10 cap are still passed to `Map_Stmap45SetSclLoadFeedbackWithEntries`. This affects high-pressure designs with critical sinks, so cap the final selected ratio before handing it to the mapper.
